2.bug_scenario:
When Prism highlights a TypeScript interface declaration, it incorrectly marks the property name “type?” as a language keyword. In the screenshot you can see an interface

export interface R<T> {
  data: T;
  total: number;
  type?: string;
}

Prism’s highlighter treats the “type” identifier on the left side of the colon as the built-in keyword “type”, instead of simply a property name.
